      "created_at": "2013-11-09T22:15:03.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I just want to make sure I have this right.&nbsp; If Illusory Demon is chosen as the target of an Ongoing that causes damage to be dealt, such as Impale, and that damage destroys the demon, since the \"when this card is destroyed\" effects resolve in card-play order, Impale's \"the target is gone, so destroy this\" doesn't happen until after the Demon's \"destroy an Ongoing\" happens, and so you can (and probably should) choose Impale as the destroyed Ongoing, just before it would be destroyed anyway.&nbsp; Agreed?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:39.693Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
